 Fish Advisories - OEHHA Skip to main content Skip to Main Content CA.gov CA.gov Official website of the State of California Reset High contrast Increase font size Font increase Decrease font size Font decrease Dyslexic font State of California OEHHA Search Menu Custom Google Search Submit Close Environmental Topics All Environmental Topics Air Climate Change Fish Pesticides Water CalEnviroScreen CalHeatScore About About OEHHA What We Do Meet the Executive Office Organizational Chart Overview of Programs Environmental Topics OEHHA Laws and Regulations Careers at OEHHA Join Our Listservs Contact Us Proposition 65 Proposition 65 Overview About Proposition 65 The Proposition 65 List Meetings, Hearings and Workshops Notices Law and Regulations Warnings News and Events Latest News Events Public Comments Library Library Overview Chemical Databases Documents Maps Prop 65 Chemical List Videos Home Fish Fish Advisories Fish Advisories Good Catch California is the OEHHA fish advisory program. We provide advice so that you can make healthy choices about eating the fish you catch. Fish Advisories are guidelines that recommend how often you can safely eat fish caught from water bodies in California. The Office of Environmental Health Hazard Assessment (OEHHA) offers over 150 site-specific advisories for lakes, rivers, bays, reservoirs, and the coast. For water bodies without site-specific advice, or for species not included in a site-specific advisory, look for the appropriate statewide advisory. OEHHA provides two sets of guidelines for eating fish, one for each of the following populations: Women 18-49 years and children 1-17 years Women 50 years and older and men 18 years and older General Information Fish Advisory Fact Sheet (PDF) English | Spanish | Simplified Chinese | Traditional Chinese | Vietnamese How to Follow Advisories Women &amp; Children General Tips Statewide Advisories California Lakes and Reservoirs without site-specific advice California Coastal Locations without site-specific advice California Rivers, Streams, and Creeks without site-specific advice Advisory for Fish that Migrate How to follow OEHHA’s Fish Consumption Advisories OEHHA’s Fish Consumption Advisories and Safe Eating Guidelines Waterbody - Any - Alamitos Creek Alamo River All-American Canal Almaden Lake Almaden Reservoir Alondra Park Lake American River, Lower Anderson Lake Antelope Lake Bass Lake Bear Creek Bear River Big Bear Lake Bishop Creek Black Butte Lake Bon Tempe Reservoir Bridgeport

